| Delegated verification | Proposal verification; inventory counts/scenarios | Final generator 36/36; focused contracts/accessors/loader/source tests 74/74; bounded GPU 4/4; normal and fresh builds retain 98 stages / 243 binaries; isolated build validator passed; no skipped tests |

Transition boundary: generated owners are excluded from the legacy discovery scan and added through generated references. Fifteen packaged programs (the 13 height-bake programs plus graphics/compute infrastructure fixtures), both isolated build-validator owners, and one separately scoped accessor fixture demonstrate the new path. The remaining owners stay on the verified legacy path until 3.3. Full runtime coherent snapshots/effective-input scheduling and exhaustive GPU/package verification remain assigned to phases 5–6. No shader algorithm, default, inventory count, binary layout parser or output cleanup policy is changed.

Completion evidence (2026-09-22): independent audit-stage-completion review confirmed all six tasks and the gate with high confidence and no outstanding findings. Source review and the second pass checked the complete inherited proposal/inventory against the mapping above. The solution lists both the generator and its test project, preserving discovery by the existing solution-level CI test command.

