### Phase 3.2: Replace named condition attributes with inline expressions

Depends on 3.1. Authority: [approved proposal — Inline condition expressions](ShaderVariantContracts.proposal.md#inline-condition-expressions) and [migration inventory — Numeric specializations](ShaderVariantContracts.inventory.md#numeric-specializations). Outcome: `ShaderUse.When` accepts a short, validated C#-style expression instead of a reference to separately named condition attributes. The existing `ShaderCondition` model remains the shared build/runtime representation.

- [x] Define the restricted expression grammar and name/type rules: structural option property references, Boolean literals, `!`, `&&`, `||`, parentheses and equality comparisons against typed constants. Support inventoried Boolean conditions and finite integer/enum equality; document supported constant spellings, precedence and null/empty handling. Resolve names against the owning class's attributed properties, including shared-option references, and require every dependency to be structural in the consuming stage. Keep GLSL names/aliases distinct from property names.
- [x] Parse expressions with Roslyn during generation, validate the allowed syntax and operand types, and lower them into the existing `ShaderCondition.Equal/All/Any/Not` model. Reject unsupported syntax, unknown properties, nonstructural dependencies, invalid constants and trailing/malformed input with diagnostics identifying the owner, stage and expression. Do not compile or execute expressions, allow arbitrary member access/calls, or add a runtime expression parser.
- [x] Replace the current named-node reader and migrate all existing attributed declarations, representative fixtures and generator tests to inline `When` expressions. Remove `ShaderEqualsAttribute`, `ShaderAllAttribute`, `ShaderAnyAttribute` and `ShaderNotAttribute` plus their discovery/validation/emission handling; do not retain a parallel named-condition compatibility path. Keep existing handwritten `ShaderCondition` declarations operational until the owner migration in 3.3.
- [x] Add focused parser/generator tests for operator precedence, parentheses, nested negation, typed equality, shared-option references, malformed/unsupported expressions, renamed or unknown properties, numeric-specialization references, and diagnostic locations. Compile generated output in runtime and offline modes and verify equivalent condition trees/selections. Assert the inventoried world-probe, near-field sky fallback and importance-sampling conditions across their structural assignments, including retained inactive values and unchanged binary identity/counts.
- [x] Update attribute XML documentation, proposal examples and authoring guidance to explain expression syntax, limitations and the lack of automatic C# rename support inside strings. Run delegated generator/contract tests, a normal shader-enabled build and isolated build-contract validation. Preserve the existing 63 packaged programs / 98 stages / 242 assignments / 243 binaries and the isolated validator scopes; record new receipts separately from 3.1 evidence.

Gate:

- [x] Inline expressions are the only attributed condition-authoring mechanism; invalid expressions fail during generation, and build/runtime selection preserves the inventoried availability behavior through the existing condition model. Removed named attributes have no remaining consumers, documentation is current, and delegated verification passes. Full shader-owner migration remains in 3.3.

