Completion evidence (2026-09-22): independent audit-stage-completion review confirmed all six tasks and the gate with high confidence and no outstanding findings. The second review and audit checked declaration ownership, canonical metadata, conditional uses, caller changes, unchanged binding construction/fixed build profile, deleted discovery machinery and the current authoring guide.

Receipts under `artifacts/shader-variant-contracts`: `full-migration-generator.log/.trx` (88 passed), `full-migration-build-v2.log` (98 stages / 243 variants, zero errors), `full-migration-focused-v2.log/.trx` (71 passed), `full-migration-gpu.log/.trx` (five passed), and `full-migration-build-contract.log` (PASS; detailed `artifacts/spirv-build-contract/run-20260922-145808/result.txt`). No tests were skipped. The focused suite now replaces nine obsolete reflection-discovery cases with six generated-catalog/baseline/production-accessor cases, and confirms 63 packaged programs / 98 stages / 242 assignments / 243 binaries plus isolated scopes. The new GPU case exercises a production generated property through queued successful replacement and failed replacement preservation; the other four retain graphics lifecycle, compute and ring-buffer coverage.

The 1,111-row fixture was captured from the previously compiled assembly before rebuilding (`full-migration-baseline-capture.json` records its hash/time). It preserves program budgets, groups, defaults, types, aliases, domains, stage identities, specialization IDs, every finite availability assignment and binary paths. Its first comparison exposed culture-versus-ordinal ordering in the PowerShell capture; only within-row ordering was normalized, without changing semantic values or regenerating expectations from migrated declarations. The raw pre-normalization bytes were not separately retained. The exact normalized snapshot comparison passes. The initial build's alias-array syntax typo was corrected before the passing build. Remaining warnings were unavailable NuGet vulnerability-feed diagnostics and existing test-analyzer warnings.

Transition boundary: `LegacyShaderStageContract` still adapts generated contracts for the builder/source emitter and stage loader. Direct-file compute addressing and the public string setter retain their documented compatibility behavior until the loader/runtime migration. Typed writes now preserve exact scalar values rather than formatting floats through caller-specific decimal strings. Generated accessors retain inactive selections; existing resource-driven topology helpers still explicitly publish their existing disabled sentinels. No new compiler, binary-reflection, runtime-manifest or cleanup machinery was added. Full mod packaging, exhaustive GPU execution and live-game behavior remain unclaimed and assigned to later work.
## Phase 4: Contract-driven build and AST emission

Depends on phase 3.3. Outcome: the builder compiles deduplicated stage configurations from the generated catalog and publishes unchanged compiler binaries.

- [x] Migrate `ShaderVariantBuild` to enumerate supported program configurations, project them to stages, and compile each unique stage configuration once. Report program-combination and stage-binary counts separately. Source enumeration reports unregistered owned entry points without inventing contracts.
- [x] Update `ShaderVariantSource` to use typed fixed/structural values and active specialization declarations. Use shared condition evaluation and stable IDs, preserving macro mappings and omitting inactive declarations/overrides.
- [x] Retain import expansion through `ShaderSyntaxTreePreprocessor`, then use existing VGE GLSL schema/TinyAst editing to insert configuration before uses and guarded defaults. Keep GLSL conditional evaluation in the compiler and keep `ShaderSourceLayout` responsible for declared layouts.
- [x] Replace the remaining derived-global-constant regex rewriting with a separate syntax-aware implementation. Inspect existing schema specializations before extending them; preserve comments, nested expressions, function-local constants, and actual source behavior.
- [x] Preserve default and deterministic nondefault paths, strict binary publication, and build-receipt invalidation for contracts/source/fixed defines/bindings/tool inputs. Keep the receipt out of runtime assets; do not add manifests or binary instruction parsing.
- [x] Add source-emission tests for typed macros, conditional specializations, guarded imported defaults, and derived-global-constant transformations. Assert our transformations rather than interpreting compiler binaries.
- [x] Update/run `ValidateBuildContract.ps1` with registered fixtures and the new inventory. Verify unchanged compiler bytes, incremental invalidation, deduplication, complete asset coverage, and fresh package contents without runtime metadata.
- [x] Run the normal shader-enabled build and compile all declared configurations. Attribute any change from the baseline inventory to deliberate declarations/deduplication rather than silently losing variants.

Gate:

- [x] Every declared stage configuration compiles once, every expected binary exists at its resolved path, and the source/build/package checks pass. Runtime can consume the new output through the verified transition path; no temporary parallel catalogs are required.

